%description:

A deviation of StochasticChannelModel from the specification, pinned and not
endorsed: when an end of
a link has moved farther than the LOS correlation distance, the link's LOS state
is drawn again, independently of the state it had and of where it had it.

TR 38.901 v16.1.0 7.6.3.3: "The LOS state can be determined according to the
spatial consistency procedure for random variables as mentioned in Clause
7.6.3.1, by comparing a realization of a random variable generated with
distance-dependent LOS probability. If the realization is less than the LOS
probability, the state is LOS; otherwise NLOS." 7.6.3.1: "The procedure can be
considered as a 2D random process (in the horizontal plane) given the UT
locations based on the parameter-specific correlation distance values for
spatial consistency, specified in Table 7.6.3.1-2." The model takes the table's
distance (UMa: 50 m) as the displacement beyond which it draws again, but each
draw is a new uniform number, not a value of a process over the UT's location.

Checked on a UMa cell, on fifty outdoor UEs, each evaluated 100 m from the base
station, then 60 m farther out, then at the first place again. Every evaluation
draws: the state at each step is the next number of the model's generator,
replayed from a copy, against the LOS probability at that place. So a UE back at
its first place need not have the state it had there: some of the fifty differ.
ChannelModelLosSpatialConsistencySpec asserts the consequence of the
specification as an expected failure. When the model follows it, change this
test together with that one.

%includes:
#include "SchedulerTestUtil.h"
#include "ChannelModelTestUtil.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;
using inet::Coord;

%file: harness.ned
import simu5g.common.binder.Binder;
import simu5g.stack.phy.medium.CellularRadioMedium;
import simu5g.common.carrierAggregation.CarrierAggregation;
import simu5g.stack.phy.channelmodel.Tr38901ChannelModel;

network Harness
{
    submodules:
        binder: Binder;
        radioMedium: CellularRadioMedium;
        carrierAggregation: CarrierAggregation;
        channelModel: Tr38901ChannelModel;
        test: Test;
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = Harness
cmdenv-express-mode = false
cmdenv-log-prefix = ""
sim-time-limit = 1s
*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 1
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 10
**.cellInfoModule = ""
*.binder.printTrafficGeneratorConfig = false

# the LOS state is drawn, at the study's correlation distance (UMa: 50 m); the
# first number an evaluation that decides the state draws is the state's
**.dynamicLos = true
**.shadowing = false
**.fading = false

%no-default-inifile: 1

%activity:
Checker c;
auto *model = harnessModule<StochasticChannelModel>(this, "channelModel");
auto *medium = harnessModule<CellularRadioMedium>(this, "radioMedium");
ChannelModelProbe probe(model);

// a UMa base station and fifty outdoor UEs, each a link of its own
const int numUes = 50;
const Coord home(100, 0, 1.5), away(160, 0, 1.5);   // 60 m apart: more than the 50 m
StubEndpoint bs;
bs.nodeId = MacNodeId(1);
bs.coord = Coord(0, 0, 25);
StubRadioRegistration bsRadio(medium, bs.nodeId, &bs);
std::vector<std::unique_ptr<StubEndpoint>> ues;
std::vector<std::unique_ptr<StubRadioRegistration>> ueRadios;
for (int i = 0; i < numUes; i++) {
    ues.push_back(std::make_unique<StubEndpoint>());
    ues[i]->nodeId = MacNodeId(1025 + i);
    ueRadios.push_back(std::make_unique<StubRadioRegistration>(medium, ues[i]->nodeId, ues[i].get()));
}
auto losProbabilityAt = [&] (const Coord& position) {
    return probe.pathLoss()->computeLosProbability(probe.deployment(25, 1.5), bs.coord.distance(position),
            std::hypot(position.x - bs.coord.x, position.y - bs.coord.y));
};

wait(0.010);

// The LOS state of a UE's downlink evaluated with the UE at a position, and
// the state an independent draw gives there: the next number of the model's
// generator, replayed from a copy, against the LOS probability at the position.
struct Evaluation { bool los; bool independentDraw; };
auto evaluateAt = [&] (int i, const Coord& position) {
    ues[i]->coord = position;
    RadioLink link = probe.whatIfLink(ues[i].get(), dlCqiTransmission(&bs, ues[i]->nodeId));
    RngSnapshot snapshot(model);
    model->getAttenuation(link);
    bool los = probe.losMap().at(link.stateKey()).los;
    return Evaluation{los, omnetpp::uniform(snapshot.rng(), 0.0, 1.0) <= losProbabilityAt(position)};
};

// each UE is evaluated at home, then 60 m away, then at home again
int numIndependentAway = 0, numIndependentBack = 0, numSameBack = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < numUes; i++) {
    Evaluation first = evaluateAt(i, home);
    Evaluation there = evaluateAt(i, away);
    Evaluation back = evaluateAt(i, home);
    numIndependentAway += (there.los == there.independentDraw);
    numIndependentBack += (back.los == back.independentDraw);
    numSameBack += (back.los == first.los);
}

c.expectValue("PINNED DEFECT: 60 m from where its state was drawn, a link's LOS state is an independent draw against the LOS probability there, for every link", numIndependentAway, numUes);
c.expectValue("PINNED DEFECT: ...and back at the first place it is an independent draw again", numIndependentBack, numUes);
c.check("PINNED DEFECT: ...so some UEs do not have the state they had at that place before", numSameBack < numUes, std::to_string(numSameBack) + " of " + std::to_string(numUes) + " the same");

c.summary();

%contains: stdout
modelchecks=3 modelfailures=0

%not-contains: stdout
FAILED
